# The servo-side position gains, loaded once at process setup and written into
# the nine servos when the session commissions the machine.
#
# Protobuf text of `brenn_reachy.cogs.config_clk_proto.ServoGains`, which the
# compiler generates from the `ServoGains` schema in `config.clk`. Read as it
# is: the box binds it by path, and the casing converts it to the message the
# dial hands the cog.
#
# One class per triple, stated as nine flat keys. The classes are three
# different loads: the legs carry the head's weight through a six-bar linkage
# and the other three carry almost nothing, so they are not tuned alike. Flat
# keys rather than a nested per-class message because every reader here is a
# first-match `key: value` line scan.
#
# The motion library states the same triples as its own default, which is what
# the simulated register file answers a gains read with and what the unit tests
# are written against; the scenario suite pins this file to that default, so a
# rung tuned here and not there is a failed run rather than a machine
# commissioned with numbers nobody wrote down.

# A proportional term alone cannot hold the head's weight up this linkage: at
# the vendor's P-only 300 the two most loaded cranks park 3.9-4.3 degrees short
# of their goal and stay there. The integral term is what closes that, and the
# derivative term is what stops it hunting; measured, the pair settles inside
# 1.3 degrees with no oscillation.
legs_p: 800
legs_i: 100
legs_d: 300

# The value the vendor's own stack writes at startup, and now a measured one.
# The yaw is gain-bound rather than motor-bound -- it reached 48 velocity units
# on the capability tour where the legs reached 326 -- so a stiffer loop was the
# obvious rung, and it was walked P-only over the wake gesture's 17 s stow hold:
# 400 limit-cycles at 3.0 counts, 8-11 Hz apparent, in three holds of three;
# 800 in one of three; 200 sits at 2.0 counts of dither, inside the stillness
# watch's two-count bound. A P-only ladder is non-monotonic here, so it stopped
# at the vendor's value.
#
# TODO(body-yaw-gains): the derivative term is the next rung -- damping is what
# a P-only ladder had nothing of -- read from `hold-probe <yaw id> --gains` and
# from a motion run that produces the long stow hold.
body_yaw_p: 200
body_yaw_i: 0
body_yaw_d: 0

# The vendor's own triple, and the measured one. Walked over the antenna step
# probes -- one commanded frame per pose, so the servo's own generator makes the
# whole move and stops it -- with every hold judged by the stillness watch where
# the head stood still, six runs a rung and six rungs:
#
# - Quiet at the sides pose and at the leaned up pose in every judged hold on
#   record, 0-1 counts against the two-count bound.
# - 200 is the proportional bound. At 400 the up pose hunts at 14-15 counts and
#   the down pose on both antennas at 8-10; at 300 the rest hold hunts at
#   7-9 counts; the shipped 500 / 0 / 100 hunts the rest hold at 9 counts and
#   12.7 Hz. The cycle's amplitude grows with the proportional term at every
#   pose that hunts.
# - The pose selects the hunt, not the arrival. At the vendor's own antenna fold
#   the down pose hunted at 7-8 counts and 10-11 Hz at every profile pair from
#   the motor's measured ceiling to the shipped floor, and halving the
#   deceleration four times moved the arrival by seconds and the excursion by
#   nothing. Gravity loads no side of the gearbox backlash at a vertical, which
#   is why the fold now leans (`disarm.rs`' STOW_ANTENNAS) as the raised pose
#   already did: at the leaned fold the same rung is quiet in six of six runs,
#   with the cycle still visible in the arrival's settle allowance and gone from
#   the judged hold.
#
# No integral term: an antenna holds nothing up, so there is no weight to
# integrate away. The cost is a parking error -- with no integral term the loop
# stops where friction balances the proportional push -- and it is measured: the
# right antenna parks 0.026 rad (16-17 counts) short at the sides pose on the
# arrival from the fold, on a hold whose excursion is inside a count, at two
# profile pairs alike.
#
# TODO(antenna-hold-gains): the integral term at this proportional term is the
# rung nobody has walked, against that parking error.
antennas_p: 200
antennas_i: 0
antennas_d: 0
